.Dd July 19, 2026
.Dt JG-LINT 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm jg-lint
.Nd lint JavaScript, TypeScript, and CoffeeScript files
.
.\"=============================================================================
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl 5CWabcjmqtw
.Op Fl E Ar eslint-options
.Op Ar paths
.
.\"=============================================================================
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.de QQ
.	ie t .Ql \\$*
.	el   .Dq \\$*
..
.Nm
is a wrapper for linting JavaScript projects,
or those written in languages that transpile to JavaScript
.Pq specifically, TypeScript and CoffeeScript .
Its main job is to ensure that the linter programs it executes use the configs \
bundled with
.Nm ,
irrespective of the current working directory.
Commands executed by
.Nm
are echoed to the standard error stream unless the
.Fl q
flag is passed;
linting stops with the first command that exits with a non-zero status.
.Pp
By default,
.Nm
scans the current working directory for files it recognises as lintable.
A list of
.Ar paths
may be specified instead,
which either point to directories to scan,
or individual files to lint.
.
.\"=============================================================================
.Sh OPTIONS
.ds eslint-version v8.57.1
.Ss Linter selection
.Bl -tag -width 6n
.It Fl j , Fl -js
Enable JavaScript linting.
Requires ESLint \*[eslint-version].
.
.It Fl t , Fl -ts
Enable TypeScript linting.
Requires ESLint \*[eslint-version];
prior to January 18, 2024,
the long-obsolete TSLint was required instead.
.
.It Fl c , Fl -coffee
Enable CoffeeScript linting.
Requires CoffeeLint v2.1.0.
.Pp
.Sy Nota bene :
that due to the obsolescence of CoffeeScript in favour of TypeScript \
and modern JavaScript,
CoffeeLint isn't installed as a dependency of
.Xr jg 1
by
.Xr npm 1 ,
and thus needs to be installed manually.
This is unlikely to impact contributors on most projects;
support for CoffeeScript linting was originally added as a means of enforcing \
indentation and formatting style in CSON
.Pq CoffeeScript Object Notation
files,
which remain in widespread use for authoring TextMate-compatible grammars.
.Nm
no longer scans for
.Li .cson
files linting CoffeeScript,
due to the limitations of CoffeeLint making it inadequate for accommodating \
the formatting style employed by the author when penning TextMate-compatible \
grammars.
.El
.Pp
If none of the above options are given,
then
.Nm
lints everything it has a linter for:
JavaScript,
TypeScript,
and CoffeeScript
.Pq in that order .
.
.Ss General options
.Bl -tag -width 6n
.It Fl q , Fl -no-echo
Don't print external commands as they're executed.
.
.It Fl w , Fl -warnings
Enable lint warnings
.Pq ignorable messages about Em potential No issues
in addition to errors
.Pq messages about issues that require fixing .
By default,
.Nm
only displays error-level messages.
.
.It Fl W , Fl -fatal-warnings
Same as the
.Fl w
switch described above,
only warnings are treated as errors,
and will thus cause
.Nm
to exit with a non-zero status.
.El
.
.Ss ESLint options
.Bl -tag -width 6n
.It Fl 5 , Fl -es5
Run ESLint with settings optimised for ECMAScript\~5 syntax.
.
.It Fl a , Fl -atom
Run ESLint with settings optimised for Atom projects.
.
.It Fl b , Fl -babel
Run ESLint with Babel transpilation.
Necessary for projects that utilise cutting-edge ECMAScript features.
.
.It Fl C , Fl -ignore-config
Ignore whatever ESLint configs are in the working directory,
even those that extend
.Sy @alhadis/eslint-config
.Pq the base configuration file bundled with Nm jg .
.
.It Fl E , Fl -eslint-options Ar opts
Arbitrary options prepended to the argument list ESLint is called with.
The
.Ar opts
value is a quoted list of shell-compatible options passed without \
interpretation to the ESLint command.
For example:
.Bd -literal -offset 4m
.Nm jg Cm lint Fl -js Fl E Qo \
--global=EAL --parser-options ecmaVersion:2019 \
 Qc Pa ./eal/lib/*.mjs
.Ed
.
.It Fl m , Fl -mw
Run ESLint with settings optimised for MediaWiki user scripts.
.El
.
.\"=============================================================================
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width 4n
.It Ev DEBUG
If non-empty,
enables the display of non-essential information about the \
running command\(cqs state.
.It Ev ESLINT_USE_FLAT_CONFIG
If set to
.QQ false ,
prevents ESLint from using flat configuration files
.Pq Pa eslint.config.\& Ns Brq Ns Pa js , Ns Pa mjs , Ns Pa cjs
in the current directory or one of its ancestors.
.It Ev FORCE_COLOR
Force ANSI-coloured output when output is redirected.
By default,
coloured output is only used if standard output is connected to a terminal; \
setting this environment variable to a supported value
.Po
.QQ 1 ,
.QQ 2 ,
.QQ 3 ,
.QQ true ,
or the empty string
.Pc ,
will force colourised output irrespective of redirection.
See
.Xr node 1
for the meanings of the aforementioned values.
.El
.
.\"=============================================================================
.Sh FILES
.ds coffee-config etc/coffeelint.json
The following file paths are relative to
.Nm jg Ap s
installation directory.
.
.Bl -tag -width 4n
.It Pa eslint/.eslintrc.json
The base ESLint configuration used for linting JavaScript by default.
.It Pa eslint/atom.js
An extension of
.Pa .eslintrc.json
optimised for linting Atom projects.
Enabled by the
.Fl a
switch.
.It Pa eslint/babel.js
An extension of
.Pa .eslintrc.json
that enables Babel transpilation in ESLint.
Enabled by the
.Fl b
switch.
.It Pa eslint/es5.json
An extension of
.Pa .eslintrc.json
optimised for linting ECMAScript\~5 syntax.
Enabled by the
.Fl 5
switch.
.It Pa eslint/mw.js
An extension of
.Pa eslint/es5.json
optimised for linting ResourceLoader-friendly MediaWiki scripts.
Enabled by the
.Fl m
switch.
.It Pa eslint/typescript.json
An extension of
.Pa .eslintrc.json
designed for linting TypeScript files,
including declaration files
.Pq those ending in Li .d.ts .
Enabled automatically by the
.Fl t
flag.
.It Pa eslint/typescript.full.json
An extension of
.Pa eslint/typescript.json
with more elaborate rules for linting TypeScript files.
Not used by default because the TypeScript files normally linted by
.Nm
are declaration files,
as this author rarely programs in TypeScript.
No switch exists to enable this config from the command-line;
its usage requires a project's local
.Pa .eslintrc.json
file to extend
.Sy @alhadis/eslint-config/typescript.full .
.It Pa \*[coffee-config]
Configuration file used by CoffeeLint for linting CoffeeScript files.
.El
.
.\"=============================================================================
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
Typically,
this will be the error code returned by a linter \
which reported one or more problems.
However,
an error code of 1 is returned if required linter(s) aren't installed
.Pq or Do reachable Dc from the user's Ev PATH .
.
.\"=============================================================================
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr jg 1 ,
.Xr jg-lint 3
.
.\"=============================================================================
.Sh HISTORY
.Nm
was written out of need for a JavaScript-based wrapper that would correctly \
call the appropriate linter programs with the author's preferred configuration.
A shell-script was insufficient,
as the linters in question needed to run on Windows-based systems
.Pq primarily as automated tasks running on CI services like Appveyor .
The aforementioned configuration files would later be bundled alongside
.Nm ,
situated in a separate directory from which new releases of a \
shareable ESLint config could be published,
albeit without an accompanying
.Xr git-tag 1 .
This shareable config was originally published to NPM out of necessity,
albeit reluctantly,
after ESLint deprecated the use of
.Dq personal
config files \(en ones located in the user's home directory
.Pq Pa ~/.eslintrc ,
which ESLint formerly loaded in addition to project-specific configurations.
.
